---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="FAQ | Institute of Property">
  <div class="py-16 px-6 sm:px-12 bg-background min-h-screen">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose prose-slate">
      <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>

      <h3>Do I need a limited company to invest in property?</h3>
      <p>It depends entirely on your tax bracket. Basic rate taxpayers often still buy in their own name. Higher rate taxpayers usually use an SPV (Special Purpose Vehicle) limited company due to Section 24 restrictions. See our <a href="/reference/limited-company/">Limited Company Guide</a>.</p>

      <h3>What is a good rental yield?</h3>
      <p>A "good" yield depends on the strategy. For a standard single-let, 5-7% gross is common. For an HMO, investors target 10-15% gross, though the net yield is often much lower due to higher operational costs.</p>

      <h3>Can I get a buy-to-let mortgage as a first-time buyer?</h3>
      <p>It is possible, but lenders view it as higher risk. You will typically need a larger deposit (25%+) and may face stricter affordability criteria.</p>

      <h3>What happens if interest rates rise?</h3>
      <p>Your cash flow decreases. This is why you must stress-test your investments using a <a href="/tools/mortgage-calculator/">mortgage calculator</a> at 6%, 7%, and 8% before buying.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
